 enjoyed it, which is great! Given your reading pace and interest in historical fiction, I think you\\'ll appreciate \"The Women in the Castle\" by Jessica Shattuck. Here\\'s why:\\n\\n**Similarities with \"The Nightingale\"**:\\n\\n1. **Historical Fiction**: Both novels are set during WWII, exploring the experiences of women during wartime.\\n2. **Emotional Depth**: Both books delve into the emotional struggles of the characters, making them relatable and engaging.\\n3. **Strong Female Characters**: Both novels feature strong, complex female characters who drive the story forward.\\n\\n**Differences and Similarities with Your Reading Pace**:\\n\\n1. **Page Count**: \"The Women in the Castle\" has 352 pages, which is slightly shorter than \"The Nightingale\". Given your reading pace of 440 pages in 5 weeks, you might finish this book in around 4-4.5 weeks.\\n2. **Writing Style**: Jessica Shattuck\\'s writing is lyrical and evocative, but slightly more introspective than Kristin Hannah\\'s. You might find the pace of the story slightly slower, but still engaging.\\n3. **Character Focus**: While \"The Nightingale\" focuses on the relationship between two sisters, \"The Women in the Castle\" explores the lives of three women, each with their own unique story. This might appeal to you if you enjoy character-driven novels.\\n\\n**Additional Reasons to Enjoy \"The Women in the Castle\"**:\\n\\n1. **Well-Researched**: Shattuck\\'s novel is meticulously researched, providing a detailed and accurate portrayal of life in Germany during WWII.\\n2. **Unique Perspective**: The book offers a fresh perspective on the war, focusing on the experiences of women in Germany, rather than those in occupied France or other countries.\\n3. **Themes**: The novel explores themes of guilt, shame, redemption, and the power of female friendships, which might resonate with you if you enjoyed the emotional depth of \"The Nightingale\".\\n\\nOverall, I think you\\'ll appreciate \"The Women in the 